WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.033
Use this framework with one specific property in front of you.

00:00:04.033 --> 00:00:11.000
Before you examine the sales case, write down the outcome the property must deliver and your intended holding period.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:13.248
Check one: objective fit.

00:00:13.248 --> 00:00:22.800
If you cannot define what success means, you cannot test whether the property belongs in your plan.

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:25.689
Check two: the full financial commitment.

00:00:25.689 --> 00:00:33.874
Put the price beside every payment, charge, finance cost, fit-out cost and continuing cost you can establish.

00:00:33.874 --> 00:00:35.800
Mark anything still estimated.

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:37.174
Check three: evidence.

00:00:37.174 --> 00:00:39.923
Separate every claim from its source.

00:00:39.923 --> 00:00:48.168
Record the date, the document or dataset, and whether it relates to this property or a different reference.

00:00:48.168 --> 00:00:50.000
Repetition is not evidence.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:52.241
Check four: competition and supply.

00:00:52.241 --> 00:00:56.724
Identify what the same buyer or tenant can choose now.

00:00:56.724 --> 00:01:03.000
Then record the relevant completed stock and future supply expected during your holding period.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:04.393
Check five: exit.

00:01:04.393 --> 00:01:16.000
Define the future buyer or tenant, why this property may remain relevant to them, what they can afford, and the strongest alternative they could choose.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:23.467
Finish with three lines: what appears supported, what remains unproven, and the next decision to make.

00:01:23.467 --> 00:01:30.000
If one line is unclear, you have identified exactly what must be established next.
